==Russian==
===Etymology===
From [[Old Church Slavonic]] '''нога''' ([[foot]]) < Proto-Indo-European ''*(o)nogʰ-'' ‘claw, nail’. Cognate with English ''[[nail]]'', Latvian ''[[nagas]]'', Latin ''[[unguis]]'', Welsh ''[[ewin]]''.

===Noun===
'''нога''' (nogá) {{f}}

#[[leg]]
#[[foot]]

===Usage notes===
Pronunciation of the genitive plural [[ног]] as “нох” is considered old-fashioned.

